  "_comment": "Pascha-relative lectionary. Keys are integer day-offsets from Orthodox Pascha (negative = before Pascha, 0 = Pascha itself, positive = after). A Sunday n weeks before Pascha is keyed -7n, so Palm Sunday is -7 and Lazarus Saturday is -8; Holy Week runs -6 through -1. Each entry is the appointed liturgical reading(s) for that day. Sundays of the Triodion (pre-Lent + Lent) and Pentecostarion (Pascha to the Sunday of All Saints) carry distinct readings, as do Holy Week and Ascension. Ordinary weekday and ferial readings drop in a content patch.",
